<title>PHILIPPINES: MUSIC debut at 7.10 pesos vs 6.30 offer.</title>
<headline>MUSIC debut at 7.10 pesos vs 6.30 offer.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>High-technology stock MUSIC Semiconductor Corp made it debut on the Philippine Stock Exchange at 7.10 pesos per share, up from its offer price of 6.30 pesos, brokers said.</p>
<p>Initial trade amounted to 396,000 shares and within the first few minutes the stock climbed to 7.70 pesos.  </p>
<p>The company manufactures computer networking products.</p>
<p>It sold 123,594,930 shares to the public starting last August 29.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 632 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
</text>
